stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> GENERATED: D1 output returns through the chokepoint with a registered use case
    GENERATED --> BLOCKED: D2 interceptor, citation, scope or format check fails
    GENERATED --> PRESENTED: D3 guardrails pass, shown to the requesting human
    PRESENTED --> PRESENTED: D4 human edits free prose, engine-bound fields stay locked
    PRESENTED --> SIGNED_OFF: D5 named human signs off from an interactive session
    PRESENTED --> DISCARDED: D6 human discards
    PRESENTED --> EXPIRED: D7 a ledger, rule, policy or target version changes
    SIGNED_OFF --> EXPIRED: D7 a ledger, rule, policy or target version changes
    SIGNED_OFF --> PRESENTED: D8 content edited after sign-off, signature voided
    SIGNED_OFF --> CHECK_PENDING: D9 target is a maker-checker point
    CHECK_PENDING --> APPLIED: D10 a distinct checker approves
    CHECK_PENDING --> PRESENTED: D11 checker returns it with reasons
    SIGNED_OFF --> APPLIED: D12 authority re-checked, applied through the human write path
    PRESENTED --> EXPIRED: D13 open longer than the draft age limit
    BLOCKED --> [*]
    DISCARDED --> [*]
    EXPIRED --> [*]
    APPLIED --> [*]

    note right of SIGNED_OFF
      The signer becomes the maker of record.
      The AI is never maker, signer or checker.
      A sign-off binds to the content hash shown.
    end note

    note right of APPLIED
      From here the object follows its own
      machine - payroll month, filing, appraisal.
      A later correction is that machine's
      business, never a re-application.
    end note
